The defense of Black's knight on c6 simply does not hold together. The attack from White's knight on e5 and the bishop on b5 is met only by Black's pawn on b7. That defender is overloaded — it cannot cover everything at once. If the captures start, the attacker comes out ahead by about two pawns. The engine confirms it: Bxc6 bxc6 Nxc6, winning about 1.9 pawns. Meanwhile, nobody is watching Black's rook on a8 right now.
